# =============================================================================
#  OPA2000 hardware project - parent repository
#
#  Tracks the hardware design sources (schematics, PCB, BOM, EDA projects).
#  The firmware projects under Code_2/ are registered as git submodules, so
#  their own build trees are ignored here as well - a submodule's .gitignore
#  already covers its own tree, but these rules keep the parent repo clean
#  while a submodule is not yet initialised.
# =============================================================================

# --- Firmware submodules ------------------------------------------------------
# Code_2/* are real git submodules, each with its own GitHub remote.  Listing
# them here is what stops `git add .` from recording a bare gitlink before
# `git submodule add` has properly registered them.  Once a submodule is
# registered, git ignores this rule for that path - the .gitmodules entry and
# the index gitlink take over, and its contents come from the child repo.
Code_2/OPA2000_h7/
Code_2/OPA2000_h7_Bootloader/
Code_2/OPA2000_h7_MSC_TEMPLATE/
Code_2/H7B0ZB_W25Q128_HSI_ExternalLoader/
Code_2/OPA2000_MCU_simple_test/

# --- Vendor reference material (datasheets, vendor app notes) -----------------
# 257 MB of PDFs and vendor documentation.  These are licensed third-party
# documents, not our design work, and would bloat the repo without adding
# recoverable value - they can be re-downloaded from the vendor.
reference/

# --- Build artefacts ----------------------------------------------------------
build/
cmake-build-*/
Debug/
Release/
*.o
*.obj
*.su
*.dep
*.d
*.map
*.elf
*.hex
*.bin
*.lst

# --- IDE / tooling state ------------------------------------------------------
.settings/
.vscode/
.project
.cproject
.mxproject
.trae/
.claude/
compile_commands.json

# --- EDA caches and autosaves -------------------------------------------------
# Every tool rewrites these on open; tracking them creates a diff storm.
fp-info-cache
*-cache.lib
*-bak/
*-cache/
*.bak
*-bak
_autosave-*
*.lck
*.kicad_prl
*.pro-bak
*.sch-bak
*.kicad_pcb-bak
prl_*.prl

# Word / Office lock and temp files (~$doc.docx, ~WRL1580.tmp)
~$*
~WRL*.tmp

# --- Simulation exports (regenerable, and large) ------------------------------
# The .asc in the same folder is the actual AWR design source - keep that.
# .fft is a 64 MB binary, .raw 13 MB; both are derived measurement data and
# both are re-exported from the design in seconds.
MCU_2/*.fft
MCU_2/*.raw
MCU_2/*.op.raw
MCU_2/*.plt
MCU_2/*.log
MCU_2/InteractiveBOM_*.html
RF_2/InteractiveBOM_*.html

# --- Misc ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.log
*.tmp
*.stackdump
